Relevant tables / columns & why they matter  
• countries.country_id : joins French customers to their country.  
• countries.country_name : lets us find “France”.  
• customers.cust_id : key that joins each French shopper to the sales table.  
• customers.country_id : connects customers to the “France” country_id.  
• sales.prod_id / cust_id / time_id / channel_id / promo_id / amount_sold : monthly sales at line level that must be filtered & aggregated.  
• promotions.promo_id : joins to sales.  
• promotions.promo_total_id : keep only rows where promo_total_id = 1.  
• channels.channel_id : joins to sales.  
• channels.channel_total_id : keep only rows where channel_total_id = 1.  
• times.time_id : calendar date that tells us the month & year of every sale.  
• currency.country / year / month / to_us : 2021 FX rate for turning € into USD.  
Typical conditions we’ll need  
• countries.country_name  = ‘France’  
• promotions.promo_total_id = 1  
• channels.channel_total_id = 1  
• strftime('%Y', times.time_id) IN ('2019','2020')   (and later ‘2021’)  

Below are 10 exploratory / build‑up SQLite queries (each different, all limited to 20 rows) that move step‑by‑step from simple inspection to the final projection.  

```sql
-- 1. What is France’s country_id?
SELECT DISTINCT country_id, country_name
FROM countries
WHERE country_name LIKE '%France%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Which channels satisfy channel_total_id = 1?
SELECT DISTINCT channel_id, channel_desc
FROM channels
WHERE channel_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Which promotions satisfy promo_total_id = 1?
SELECT DISTINCT promo_id, promo_name
FROM promotions
WHERE promo_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Which calendar years are present in the times table?
SELECT DISTINCT substr(time_id, 1, 4) AS year
FROM times
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Grab distinct year / month pairs we will need (2019‑2021).
SELECT DISTINCT substr(time_id, 1, 4) AS year,
                cast(substr(time_id, 6, 2) AS INTEGER) AS month
FROM times
WHERE year BETWEEN '2019' AND '2021'
ORDER BY year, month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. List products that were sold to French customers (any year).
SELECT DISTINCT s.prod_id
FROM   sales      AS s
JOIN   customers  AS c  ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Monthly 2019 sales amounts for France (by product & month) after channel / promo filters.
SELECT substr(t.time_id,1,4)  AS year,
       cast(substr(t.time_id,6,2) AS INTEGER) AS month,
       s.prod_id,
       SUM(s.amount_sold) AS amt_2019
FROM   sales       AS s
JOIN   times       AS t  ON t.time_id = s.time_id
JOIN   customers   AS c  ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries   AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN   promotions  AS p  ON p.promo_id   = s.promo_id   AND p.promo_total_id   = 1
JOIN   channels    AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
  AND  substr(t.time_id,1,4) = '2019'
GROUP  BY year, month, s.prod_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Monthly 2020 sales amounts for the same filters.
SELECT substr(t.time_id,1,4)  AS year,
       cast(substr(t.time_id,6,2) AS INTEGER) AS month,
       s.prod_id,
       SUM(s.amount_sold) AS amt_2020
FROM   sales       AS s
JOIN   times       AS t  ON t.time_id = s.time_id
JOIN   customers   AS c  ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries   AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN   promotions  AS p  ON p.promo_id   = s.promo_id   AND p.promo_total_id   = 1
JOIN   channels    AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
  AND  substr(t.time_id,1,4) = '2020'
GROUP  BY year, month, s.prod_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Compute 2019‑2020 growth rate per product & month.
WITH a19 AS (
  SELECT cast(substr(t.time_id,6,2) AS INTEGER) AS month,
         s.prod_id,
         SUM(s.amount_sold) AS amt_2019
  FROM   sales s
  JOIN   times t ON t.time_id = s.time_id
  JOIN   customers c ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
  JOIN   countries co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
  JOIN   promotions p ON p.promo_id = s.promo_id AND p.promo_total_id = 1
  JOIN   channels ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
    AND  substr(t.time_id,1,4) = '2019'
  GROUP  BY month, s.prod_id
), a20 AS (
  SELECT cast(substr(t.time_id,6,2) AS INTEGER) AS month,
         s.prod_id,
         SUM(s.amount_sold) AS amt_2020
  FROM   sales s
  JOIN   times t ON t.time_id = s.time_id
  JOIN   customers c ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
  JOIN   countries co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
  JOIN   promotions p ON p.promo_id = s.promo_id AND p.promo_total_id = 1
  JOIN   channels ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
    AND  substr(t.time_id,1,4) = '2020'
  GROUP  BY month, s.prod_id
)
SELECT a20.month,
       a20.prod_id,
       a19.amt_2019,
       a20.amt_2020,
       CASE WHEN a19.amt_2019 > 0 THEN a20.amt_2020 * 1.0 / a19.amt_2019 END AS growth_rate
FROM   a20
JOIN   a19 USING (month, prod_id)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Project 2021 monthly sales in USD, then average across products.
WITH a19 AS (
  SELECT cast(substr(t.time_id,6,2) AS INTEGER) AS month,
         s.prod_id,
         SUM(s.amount_sold) AS amt_2019
  FROM   sales s
  JOIN   times t ON t.time_id = s.time_id
  JOIN   customers c ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
  JOIN   countries co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
  JOIN   promotions p ON p.promo_id = s.promo_id AND p.promo_total_id = 1
  JOIN   channels ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
    AND  substr(t.time_id,1,4) = '2019'
  GROUP  BY month, s.prod_id
), a20 AS (
  SELECT cast(substr(t.time_id,6,2) AS INTEGER) AS month,
         s.prod_id,
         SUM(s.amount_sold) AS amt_2020
  FROM   sales s
  JOIN   times t ON t.time_id = s.time_id
  JOIN   customers c ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
  JOIN   countries co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
  JOIN   promotions p ON p.promo_id = s.promo_id AND p.promo_total_id = 1
  JOIN   channels ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
    AND  substr(t.time_id,1,4) = '2020'
  GROUP  BY month, s.prod_id
), growth AS (
  SELECT a20.month,
         a20.prod_id,
         a20.amt_2020,
         CASE WHEN a19.amt_2019 > 0 THEN (a20.amt_2020 * 1.0 / a19.amt_2019) ELSE NULL END AS growth_rate
  FROM   a20
  JOIN   a19 USING (month, prod_id)
)
SELECT g.month,
       AVG(g.amt_2020 * g.growth_rate * cu.to_us) AS avg_projected_sales_usd_2021
FROM   growth  AS g
JOIN   currency AS cu
       ON cu.country = 'France'
      AND cu.year   = 2021
      AND cu.month  = g.month
GROUP  BY g.month
ORDER  BY g.month
LIMIT 20;
```

Each successive query unpacks another required piece—locating France, filtering valid channels & promos, extracting 2019/2020 sales, computing growth, converting with 2021 FX rates, and finally averaging projected monthly USD sales.
